Chapter: RocPolyListLen
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_issue_tests.zig, "issue 9390:
 var initialized from polymorphic list.len reads back as U64":

     foo : List(a) -> U64
     foo = |list| { var $idx = list.len()   $idx }
     main = foo([0])                                              1

 A polymorphic builtin's result bound by a `let` inside a polymorphic
 definition, then read back. Called at two element types.

Section: Functions

  foo : List a -> Integer
  foo (list) =
   let idx = list-length list
   in idx

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (foo [0]))
   print-line-uni (show (foo ["a", "b"]))
  end
